# Keep the image small and clean: never copy local-only or generated files in.
.git
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.env
# Node dependencies and build output. The webapp image runs its own `npm install`
# inside the build, so a host copy is never needed — and at ~390 MB it was being
# uploaded to the Docker daemon on EVERY build of EVERY service, which is most of
# why builds here take minutes.
node_modules/
dist/
# Local backups of the environment file. Never in an image, same as .env itself.
.env.*
!.env.example

# Office documents and their LOCK FILES. Word/Excel/PowerPoint create a ~$name
# file while a document is open, and delete it on close. Docker tars the build
# context up front, so a lock file vanishing mid-tar fails the whole build with
# "Can't close tar writer: missed writing N bytes" — which is what happened on
# 2026-08-21 and silently left the API running its previous image.
#
# None of these belong in an image anyway: they are deliverables for people, not
# inputs to the service.
~$*
*.pptx
*.xlsx
*.docx
*.pdf
